Bottom line: Spatie remains an excellent, battle-tested choice for standard RBAC. Laravel Permission Manager adds the enterprise layers — hierarchy, deny rules, ABAC, tenancy depth, auditing, and debugging — that Spatie doesn't cover.
💭 Final Thoughts
Authorization anti-patterns aren't mistakes. They're the natural consequence of starting simple and scaling without a plan.
Every Laravel app begins with if ($user->is_admin). The question isn't whether you'll hit these walls — it's when, and whether you'll have the tools to climb them.
The good news? You don't have to solve them one by one. A single cohesive package can handle all ten, and give you a foundation that scales from MVP to enterprise without rewrites.
Count how many anti-patterns you recognized in your own codebase:
